<title>USA: Colo. 262 MW Rawhide coal-fired plant seen up Wed.</title>
<headline>Colo. 262 MW Rawhide coal-fired plant seen up Wed.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 262 megawatt (MW) Rawhide coal-fired power plant in northern Colorado is expected to restart Wednesday, a spokeswoman for the Platte River Power Authority said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut late Saturday for the repairs of its boiler tube, she said.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761))</p>
